{
 "about": "Which structures of Z-Anatomy's Startup.blend go into which model file of the Anatomy tab, and how much they are simplified. Read by export.py (Blender) and make_index.py. A structure is put in the first file that names it in 'objects'; otherwise in the first file one of whose 'groups' is among its ancestors (Z-Anatomy's '.g' group labels).",
 "exclude": {
  "groups": [
   "Ear.g",
   "Auditory ossicles.g",
   "Abdominopelvic cavity.g",
   "Thoracic cavity.g",
   "Fasciae.g",
   "Meninges.g",
   "Commissural fibres of telencephalon.g",
   "Projection fibres of telencephalon.g",
   "Bursae of lower limb.g",
   "Bursae of upper limb.g",
   "Tendon sheaths of lower limb.g",
   "Tendon sheaths of upper limb.g",
   "Hairs.g",
   "Regions of human body.g",
   "Joints.g",
   "Teeth.g"
  ],
  "names": [
   "^Renal pelvis",
   "^Intrarenal ",
   "^White matter of telencephalon",
   "^Stria terminalis",
   "segment of liver",
   "^\\?+$",
   "^Cochlea",
   "^Vestibule\\.",
   "semicircular",
   "^Zonular fibres",
   "-curve",
   "^Central canal'",
   "^Spinal dura",
   "^Choroid plexus"
  ],
  "why": {
   "Ear.g": "the inner ear is adapted from 'Anatomy of the Inner Ear' (University of Dundee), CC BY-NC-SA 4.0: not free for commercial use, so the whole ear is left out",
   "^Renal pelvis, ^Intrarenal": "Z-Anatomy adapted a kidney by Lissie Cowley (CC BY-NC 4.0); BodyParts3D has no renal pelvis or intrarenal vessels, so these may come from it and are left out (the kidneys themselves are BodyParts3D's)",
   "^White matter of telencephalon, fibres": "Z-Anatomy names a 'White matter' model from the University of Washington without a licence: the white matter of the hemispheres and its fibre bundles are left out",
   "others": "left out to keep the models small and clear: fasciae, meninges, peritoneum, pleura, bursae, tendon sheaths, joints, teeth, hair, regions of the body, the segments of the liver (which overlap the liver)"
  }
 },
